{
  "summary": "Adds `btck_witness_stack_to_bytes` to the libbitcoinkernel C API and C++ wrapper, serializing a witness stack into its consensus byte representation via a writer callback. It also adds unit tests verifying empty and populated witness stack serialization in `test_kernel`.",
  "problem": "Reading all items of a witness stack through libbitcoinkernel requires calling `btck_witness_stack_get_item_at` repeatedly, resulting in O(n²) retrieval costs. Callers currently have no single-call method to extract the full witness data without deserializing item by item.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"I agree the O(n²) cost of reading a whole witness with `btck_witness_stack_get_item_at` needs fixing.\"",
    "Proposed as an alternative approach to PR #36909 (\"kernel: add btck_witness_stack_get_items\"), matching existing `*_to_bytes` conventions in libbitcoinkernel."
